  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize forming the 'Eye' (identical pair) early, as it's the hardest part of the hand to complete. Keep tiles that are versatile for 'Tens' (like 5s and 6s).\n\nWatch for 'Dead Tiles': If three double-six tiles have already been discarded by others, your remaining double-six can never form an Eye and should be used in a total-sum pair instead.\n\nThe 'Wait Rule': If you draw a tile that *could* complete a 10-sum, but it's a Military tile with no matching partner left in the deck, discard it immediately to avoid 'clogging' your hand.",
    Player: "Prioritize forming the 'Eye' (identical pair) early, as it's the hardest part of the hand to complete. Keep tiles that are versatile for 'Tens' (like 5s and 6s).\n\nWatch for 'Dead Tiles': If three double-six tiles have already been discarded by others, your remaining double-six can never form an Eye and should be used in a total-sum pair instead.\n\nThe 'Wait Rule': If you draw a tile that *could* complete a 10-sum, but it's a Military tile with no matching partner left in the deck, discard it immediately to avoid 'clogging' your hand.",
